# Main UI redesign (phased)

Work ships as **six sequential phases**. Each phase ends with its own QA checklist and git branch (`phase-N-…`) per development rules. Later phases build on earlier ones.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  P1[Phase1_Layout] --> P2[Phase2_Icons]
  P2 --> P3[Phase3_Themes]
  P3 --> P4[Phase4_SettingsModal]
  P4 --> P5[Phase5_RemovePlayground]
  P5 --> P6[Phase6_ProjectSettingsNav]
```

## Decisions locked (all phases)

- **Layout target:** three panes — AppNav | ContextNav | Main (`Outlet`).
- **Theme tokens:** all colors via CSS variables; **mutable until feature-complete**.
- **Themes (shipped):** green (default), blue, orange, yellow, purple, red — picker lives under Settings (AppNav swatches removed).
- **Ideas:** top-level section only (post-it holding area); deeper Ideas UX deferred.
- **Image board:** PureRef-inspired; global stub + project **Images** stub.
- **Project middle nav:** Overview, Tasks, Kanban, Canvas, Images, Documents (Wiki); **Settings** added in Phase 6 for module enable/disable (not the app-wide Settings modal).
- **Lists:** app-nav → `/todos` (project To Dos stay on overview/⌘K).
- **App Settings modal (Phase 4):** overlay only — does not replace middle/main panes.
- **Clock:** bottom of AppNav, centered — local + `(…Z)` Zulu + weekday/date.
- **Branding sheet:** reference for wordmark (Task / Mesh) and mesh mark — not the functional icon source.
- **Icons (from Phase 2):** Font Awesome Free via `NavIcon` + `currentColor`.
- **Playground:** no longer needed for showcasing shared primitives — remove in Phase 5.

