## Phase 4 — Settings modal

**Goal:** Gear opens a **Settings modal**; move existing settings UI into it (plus theme picker from Phase 3).

### Scope

- `SettingsModal` (reuse patterns from [`ConfirmDialog`](client/src/components/ConfirmDialog.tsx) / panel chrome): overlay, focus trap, Esc to close, confirm-on-destructive already in child pages.
- **Tabs or sidebar inside modal:**
  - **Appearance** — theme picker (from Phase 3)
  - **Import / Export** — content from [`ImportExportPage`](client/src/pages/ImportExportPage.tsx)
  - **Backups** — content from [`BackupsPage`](client/src/pages/BackupsPage.tsx)
  - **Assistant** — content from [`AssistantSettingsPage`](client/src/pages/AssistantSettingsPage.tsx)
- AppNav **Settings** opens modal (not a middle-nav settings list).
- Deep links: keep `/settings/*` routes working by opening the modal to the right tab (or redirect into modal state) so ⌘K / bookmarks still work.
- Remove redundant Home buttons that only duplicated settings entry points (or point them at the modal).
- Update CommandPalette: “Settings” / per-section actions open the modal.

### Out of scope (Phase 4)

- New settings domains (auth, multi-user, etc.)
- Rewriting backup/import business logic
- Playground removal (Phase 5)

### QA (Phase 4)

- Gear opens modal; all four sections usable
- Import/export, backups schedule, assistant settings behave as before
- Theme change from Appearance persists
- Esc / backdrop closes; ⌘K settings entries open modal
- Direct `/settings/backups` (etc.) still reaches the right content

**Branch:** `phase-12d-main-ui-settings-modal`

