## Phase 5 — Remove Playground

**Goal:** Delete the shared-primitives Playground entirely — the real app shell is the showcase now.

### Scope

- Remove DEV route `/dev/playground` from [`main.tsx`](client/src/main.tsx).
- Delete [`PlaygroundPage.tsx`](client/src/pages/PlaygroundPage.tsx).
- Remove AppNav Playground link ([`AppNav.tsx`](client/src/components/shell/AppNav.tsx)).
- Remove CommandPalette “Playground” Go-to entry ([`CommandPalette.tsx`](client/src/components/CommandPalette.tsx)).
- Remove playground-only CSS (e.g. `.playground-canvas-demo` in [`index.css`](client/src/index.css)).
- Update docs that advertise the playground:
  - [`README.md`](README.md) (Shared UI playground line)
  - [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md) (Playground convention bullet; phase-delivery QA wording can drop “playground routes when applicable”)
  - Optionally soften [`.cursor/rules/development-rules.mdc`](.cursor/rules/development-rules.mdc) QA checklist language so it no longer requires `/dev/playground`
- Grep for remaining `playground` / `Playground` references and clean product-facing ones (historical executed plans may stay).

### Out of scope (Phase 5)

- Removing shared primitives themselves (`ColorPopover`, `ElementShell`, etc.) — only the playground harness goes away
- Settings modal work (Phase 4)

### QA (Phase 5)

- `/dev/playground` redirects to home (catch-all) or 404→home; no Playground in AppNav or ⌘K
- App still builds; shared components used in-product still work
- README / AGENTS no longer point users at the playground

**Branch:** `phase-12e-remove-playground`

**Note:** Can run before or after Phase 6; no dependency on project Settings nav.

