## Phase 6 — Project Settings (middle nav)

**Goal:** Move the **Project modules** enable/disable hub off the project Overview main page into a dedicated project middle-nav item **Settings**.

This is **per-project** configuration (which modules are enabled), distinct from the app-wide Settings modal (Appearance / Import / Backups / Assistant).

### Scope

- Add middle-nav item **Settings** (gear icon) when a project is selected, in [`useShellNav`](client/src/lib/useShellNav.ts) `PROJECT_MIDDLE` — e.g. last in the list after Documents (Wiki), always available (not gated on a module key).
- Route via existing tab query: `/projects/:id?tab=settings` (extend `Tab` / `TAB_ALIASES` on [`ProjectDetailPage`](client/src/pages/ProjectDetailPage.tsx); treat like `images` — no module enable check).
- Move the **Project modules** card (`.module-hub` Enable / Disable / Open controls) from the Overview tab into the new Settings main pane.
- Overview keeps project name/status/description/tags editing only — no module hub.
- Optional: “Open” on an enabled module still switches to that module tab; after Enable, navigate to the module or stay on Settings (prefer stay on Settings unless current Open behavior is clearer).
- Context nav label **Settings** must not be confused with AppNav Settings — same word is OK if scoped under the “Project” middle-nav title.

### Out of scope (Phase 6)

- App-wide Settings modal changes
- New project prefs beyond existing module toggles (color, archive, etc.) unless already on Overview and naturally belong here
- Playground removal (Phase 5)

### QA (Phase 6)

- Project middle nav shows **Settings**; selecting it shows the module hub only
- Overview no longer lists Project modules
- Enable / Disable still updates which middle-nav module items are available
- Open (or equivalent) still reaches Tasks / Kanban / etc.
- AppNav Settings still opens the app modal without changing project panes

**Branch:** `phase-12f-project-settings-nav`

